"use strict";(self.webpackChunksimrantcg=self.webpackChunksimrantcg||[]).push([[835],{835:e=>{e.exports=JSON.parse('[{"type":"title","content":"Gardevoir GX"},{"type":"image","src":"/decks/sum-lot/gardevoirgx/cover.jpg"},{"type":"imageCaption","content":"A playable Gardevoir? Never seen one."},{"type":"heading","content":"Concept"},{"type":"paragraph","content":"If Gardevoir isn\'t top of the meta, is it really a Pokemon format? A contender since its win at the 2017 World Championships, this time the Fairy-Type menace comes with pals Alolan Ninetales GX and Swampert ready to help turn a Gardevoir GX into a OHKO machine. This deck has insane draw, acceleration, recursion, a crazy high HP attacker without a damage cap, hard counters to Ultra Beasts and Spread, two capable single-prize attackers and oh my does Gardevoir not just always have everything?!"},{"type":"heading","content":"The Deck"},{"type":"image","src":"/decks/sum-lot/gardevoirgx/decklist.jpg"},{"type":"link","href":"https://my.limitlesstcg.com/builder?i=10333LOT1390133LOT1400332BUS930133LOT1410232CES320132CES340232CES350232GRI210233LOT1320232GRI600132SUM640133SMP1040433LOT1880333UPR1190233BUS1150133FLI1080133UPR1250433SUM1290433SUM1350233GRI1280133SUM1340133GRI1220233GRI1210233GRI1200731SUMY0433SUM1360133UPR136","content":"Decklist on LimitlessTCG"},{"type":"paragraph","content":"List credit goes to Jimmy Pendarvis and his group at Roanoake Regionals 2018. Modified based on suggestions from Whimsicast."},{"type":"heading","content":"Pokemon"},{"type":"subheading","content":"3-1-(3-1) Ralts, Kirlia, Gardevoir GX & Gardevoir"},{"type":"paragraph","content":"The Gardevoir line in this deck has a lot going on. Ralt\'s \u201cBeckon\u201d can be used to recycle critical Guzma and Judge against control decks, but its 50HP makes it more susceptible to a boosted Buzzwole GX \u201cJet Punch\u201d. Kirlia helps to save rare candies, and the non-GX Gardevoir\'s \u201cSensitive Ray\u201d does a solid 160 Damage for [Y][C][C] as a single-prizer when needed, although you\'d usually rather be attacking with Gardevoir GX as its absurd 230HP means it isn\'t likely to get OHKOed."},{"type":"paragraph","content":"Speaking of Gardevoir GX, the title card of the deck has 3 relevant attributes that work nicely together. The main attack you\'ll be using is \u201cInfinite Force\u201d, which scales damage based on the amount of Energy attached to both the attacking Gardevoir GX and the Defending Pokemon. With Gardevoir GX\'s Ability \u201cSecret Spring\u201d you can ramp said damage efficiently, and although your first Gardevoir GX may not OHKO each attack, the second one should be set up enough that it cuts right through anything in the Active Spot. \u201cSecret Spring\u201d has additional utility though, as you can accelerate anywhere on your board, letting you get cheeky Alolan Ninetales GX or Solgaleo GX attacks in from nought."},{"type":"paragraph","content":"The final and maybe most interesting part of Gardevoir GX\'s arsenal is its GX attack \u201cTwilight GX\u201d. For [Y], you shuffle 10 cards from your Discard pile back into your Deck. This trump card allows you to recycle finite resources like Max Potion & Rare Candy or Energy cards against control decks. Due to Gardevoir GX\'s 230HP and ramping damage, there are often positions where you know it will not get KOed and you cannot attack for KO, and so can afford to take the turn to use \u201cTwilight GX\u201d and solidify a winning position."},{"type":"subheading","content":"2-1-2 Mudkip, Marshtomp, Swampert"},{"type":"paragraph","content":"The Swampert line is a neat inclusion. As a draw engine, this deck is looking to find combos of Stage 2 & Rare Candy & Energy in one hand, so \u201cPower Draw\u201d shines at strong dig whilst discarding dead cards from the hand. At 160HP, and as a single-prizer, Swampert is often a low priority target on the Bench, which lets you get away with keeping your draw engine in play for longer."},{"type":"paragraph","content":"Notably the Swampert line was included in the deck for its Water Typing. Water-Type Mudkip can be searched via Brooklet Hill, and the Water-Type Swampert can use \u201cHydro Pump\u201d with a Super Boost Energy {*} (or a DCE, Fairy Energy & Choice Band) to OHKO Blacephalon GX, which Gardevoir GX struggles with."},{"type":"image","src":"/decks/sum-lot/gardevoirgx/swampert.jpg"},{"type":"imageCaption","content":"Swampert standing on the shoulders of giants"},{"type":"subheading","content":"2-2 Alolan Vulpix, Alolan Ninetales GX"},{"type":"paragraph","content":"With the introduction of Alolan Ninetales GX in Lost Thunder, the portion of setup decks moved to a gameplan of using \u201cBeacon\u201d followed by \u201cMysterious Guidance\u201d to flood their board with Evolution Pokemon as early as turn 2. Gardevoir GX is one of those decks. Brooklet Hill searchable Alolan Vulpix can tutor its evolution and a Gardevoir GX to hand, without even costing an Energy. This can then be followed up with a \u201cMysterious Guidance\u201d to get 2 Rare Candy, maybe the Timer Ball, anything your heart desires. And from there Alolan Ninetales GX isn\'t a dead space on the board, it is a capable attacker, softening up targets with \u201cSnowy Wind\u201d and is critical in the Blacephalon GX and Buzzwole GX matchups as \u201cSublimation GX\u201d OHKOs any Ultra-Beast."},{"type":"image","src":"/decks/sum-lot/gardevoirgx/alolatales.jpg"},{"type":"imageCaption","content":"The Alolan Vulpix/Ninetales line"},{"type":"subheading","content":"2 Tapu Lele GX"},{"type":"paragraph","content":"Tapu Lele GX is an Ultra Ball searchable out to any Supporter card in the deck with its \u201cWonder Tag\u201d Ability. Turn 1 this can grab an Elm\'s Lecture, or it can fetch the game winning Guzma on the last turn. You can also attack with \u201cEnergy Drive\u201d in a pinch, and even further ramp it with Gardevoir GX\'s \u201cSecret Spring\u201d. As the lowest HP Pokemon GX in the deck, take care to not bench it where unnecessary. "},{"type":"subheading","content":"1-0-1 Cosmog, Solgaleo GX"},{"type":"paragraph","content":"This tech inclusion shores up a number of matchups. Solgaleo GX is another behemoth at 250HP, and \u201cShining Mane\u201d removes the Weakness on all of your Pokemon in play, drastically improving the decks matchup into Metal-Type decks. Both of its attacks are solid, \u201cProminence GX\u201d primarily working to bully spread style Shrine of Punishment decks, whilst \u201cTurbo Strike\u201d threatens 2HKOs on most Pokemon GX whilst reloading a threat on your Bench."},{"type":"heading","content":"Trainers"},{"type":"subheading","content":"Elm Brooklet Engine and Setup"},{"type":"paragraph","content":"Where this deck can struggle is getting set up fast enough that your opponent cannot simply cheese a win by koing evolving Basic Pokemon and then gusting a benched Tapu Lele GX. To ensure as many Pokemon Turn 1 the deck plays a full 4 copies of Professor Elm\'s Lecture, and the 2 Brooklet Hill help search Mudkip and Alolan Vulpix specifically. Then to evolve said Pokemon it plays a full 4 copies of both Rare Candy and Ultra Ball. "},{"type":"image","src":"/decks/sum-lot/gardevoirgx/elm.jpg"},{"type":"imageCaption","content":"Elm for some combination of Ralts, Vulpix and Mudkip"},{"type":"paragraph","content":"For further Mid-Game consistency 3 Cynthia keep you drawing, whilst the 1 Lillie can be used turn 1 for a burst draw to 8 or later to refresh an emptied hand. The 1 Timer Ball and 1 Energy Loto provide flex options to search off \u201cMysterious Guidance\u201d, Timer Ball notably does not force you to discard from hand, unlike Ultra Ball."},{"type":"paragraph","content":"The 1 Timer Ball and 1 Energy Loto provide flex options to search off \u201cMysterious Guidance\u201d, Timer Ball notably does not force you to discard from hand, unlike Ultra Ball."},{"type":"subheading","content":"Other Trainers"},{"type":"paragraph","content":"This deck plays a low 2 count of Guzma, owing to Gardevoir GX\'s uncapped damage."},{"type":"paragraph","content":"2 Choice Band help reach those high numbers either for less Energy or on the single-prize attackers in the deck."},{"type":"paragraph","content":"1 Judge keeps Zoroark and control decks from building and sitting on hands against you. "},{"type":"paragraph","content":"2 Max Potion allow you to heal a damaged attacker, then accelerating Energy to it again to simply nullify the opponent\'s last attack."},{"type":"heading","content":"Energy"},{"type":"paragraph","content":"To get enough value out of  \u201cSecret Spring\u201d and hit big numbers with Gardevoir GX, we need to play enough Fairy Energy. The deck therefore plays 7. It also plays 4 Double Colorless Energy which ramp said damage twice as fast and can allow Swampert to attack easier. The deck also plays one Super Boost Energy {*}, which can be used to add a massive 120 Damage to \u201cInfinite Force\u201d or allow Swampert to attack for 160."}]')}}]);